Package: reactextract
Title: Synthetic and Real REACT Study Data with One Extraction Interface
Version: 0.6.0.9007
Authors@R: person("mathzero", email = "mathzero@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Generates fictional, disclosure-safe REACT-1 and REACT-2 survey
    data with the same variables, coding, questionnaire routing and cleaning as
    the real study data, from a checksum-pinned, disclosure-approved aggregate
    profile. Researchers and students can learn the data and develop analysis
    code outside the secure environment. Inside it, the same extraction
    interface reads the real data from caller-managed Oracle connections or
    round files using a pinned, reviewed REACT metadata dictionary. Exact source
    values are retained; approved transforms take precedence and other reviewed
    concepts use transparent source-preserving coding.
